<%# 逆質問 bubble (SPEC §2.2): the engine reported an undeterminable requirement whose
    answer a Profile field can carry. Answering re-posts the enriched profile inline.

    Styled as an ACTION, not a chat bubble. It previously used bg-primary-50, identical to
    the greeting and summary bubbles, so the one control on screen that wanted input looked
    like passive prose. The warning family is deliberate: it matches the 要確認 badge and the
    card's 「確認ポイント:」 line, so the question and the verdict it would resolve read as
    the same thread. %>
<%# data-follow-up is the stable test hook. Tests used to scope on .bg-primary-50, which
    coupled them to the palette and broke the moment this was restyled. %>
<div data-follow-up class="rounded-lg border-2 border-warning-400 bg-warning-50 px-4 py-3 text-sm">
  <p class="mb-1 text-xs font-semibold text-warning-800">回答すると判定できます</p>
  <p class="mb-3 leading-relaxed font-medium text-neutral-900"><%= question %></p>
  <%= form_with model: intake_form, url: assessment_path, id: nil,
                data: { action: "turbo:submit-start->chat#lock turbo:submit-end->chat#unlock" } do |f| %>
    <%# Re-post the full profile; only the follow-up field changes. %>
    <%= f.hidden_field :age %>
    <%= f.hidden_field :residence %>
    <%= f.hidden_field :household_size %>
    <%= f.hidden_field :prior_year_income_jpy %>
    <%= f.hidden_field :employment %>
    <%= f.hidden_field :target %>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
      <label class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">
        <%= f.radio_button field, true, class: "accent-primary-500" %>
        <span>はい</span>
      </label>
      <label class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">
        <%= f.radio_button field, false, class: "accent-primary-500" %>
        <span>いいえ</span>
      </label>
      <%= f.submit "回答して再判定",
            class: "cursor-pointer rounded-md bg-primary-500 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-primary-400 active:bg-primary-700 disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-60" %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
